{"author":"Robert Jamieson, A. R. Fausset and David Brown","book":"Commentary Critical and Explanatory on the Whole Bible","chapter":490,"classification":{"bucket":"Christian Classics / Commentaries","canonicalStatus":"noncanonical","contentKind":"commentary","cautionReason":"","doctrinalStatus":"historical","labels":["christian-classics","commentaries"],"severity":0},"id":"classics:jfb:Ps.12","lineage":[],"metadata":{"author":"Robert Jamieson, A. R. Fausset and David Brown","authorshipDateRange":"19th century","genre":"Commentaries","tradition":"Protestant","translator":null,"edition":"1871 one-volume text; expanded electronic edition by Ernie Stefanik","rights":"Public Domain","source":{"id":"jfb","provider":"CCEL","sourceUrl":"https://www.ccel.org/ccel/jamieson/jfb.html","title":"Commentary Critical and Explanatory on the Whole Bible"},"searchIndexed":false},"originalBook":"Psalms","sourceVolumeId":"jfb","source":{"id":"jfb","sourceUrl":"https://www.ccel.org/ccel/jamieson/jfb.html","title":"Commentary Critical and Explanatory on the Whole Bible"},"title":"Psalms 12","reference":"Psalms 12","notes":[],"verses":[{"verse":1,"text":"PSALM 12","sourceParagraph":1},{"verse":2,"text":"Ps 12:1-8.","sourceParagraph":2,"scriptureVerseStart":1,"scriptureVerseEnd":1},{"verse":3,"text":"On title, see Introduction and see on Ps 6:1.","sourceParagraph":2,"scriptureVerseStart":1,"scriptureVerseEnd":1},{"verse":4,"text":"The Psalmist laments the decrease of good men.","sourceParagraph":2,"scriptureVerseStart":1,"scriptureVerseEnd":1},{"verse":5,"text":"The pride and deceit of the wicked provokes God's wrath, whose promise to avenge the cause of pious sufferers will be verified even amidst prevailing iniquity.","sourceParagraph":2,"scriptureVerseStart":1,"scriptureVerseEnd":1},{"verse":6,"text":"1. the faithful—or literally, \"faithfulness\" (Ps 31:23).","sourceParagraph":3,"scriptureVerseStart":1,"scriptureVerseEnd":1},{"verse":7,"text":"2.","sourceParagraph":4,"scriptureVerseStart":2,"scriptureVerseEnd":2},{"verse":8,"text":"The want of it is illustrated by the prevalence of deceit and instability.","sourceParagraph":4,"scriptureVerseStart":2,"scriptureVerseEnd":2},{"verse":9,"text":"3, 4.","sourceParagraph":5,"scriptureVerseStart":3,"scriptureVerseEnd":3},{"verse":10,"text":"Boasting (Da 7:25) is, like flattery, a species of lying.","sourceParagraph":5,"scriptureVerseStart":3,"scriptureVerseEnd":3},{"verse":11,"text":"lips, and … tongue—for persons.","sourceParagraph":6,"scriptureVerseStart":3,"scriptureVerseEnd":3},{"verse":12,"text":"5.","sourceParagraph":7,"scriptureVerseStart":5,"scriptureVerseEnd":5},{"verse":13,"text":"The writer intimates his confidence by depicting God's actions (compare Ps 9:19; 10:12) as coming to save the poor at whom the wicked sneer (Ps 10:5).","sourceParagraph":7,"scriptureVerseStart":5,"scriptureVerseEnd":5},{"verse":14,"text":"6.","sourceParagraph":8,"scriptureVerseStart":6,"scriptureVerseEnd":6},{"verse":15,"text":"The words—literally, \"saying of\" (Ps 12:5).","sourceParagraph":8,"scriptureVerseStart":6,"scriptureVerseEnd":6},{"verse":16,"text":"seven times—thoroughly (Da 3:19).","sourceParagraph":9,"scriptureVerseStart":6,"scriptureVerseEnd":6},{"verse":17,"text":"7. them—(Margin.)","sourceParagraph":10,"scriptureVerseStart":7,"scriptureVerseEnd":7},{"verse":18,"text":"8.","sourceParagraph":11,"scriptureVerseStart":8,"scriptureVerseEnd":8},{"verse":19,"text":"The wicked roam undisturbed doing evil, when vileness and vile men are exalted.","sourceParagraph":11,"scriptureVerseStart":8,"scriptureVerseEnd":8}],"scriptureReference":{"book":"Psalms","chapter":12}}